From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] the NTSC and PAL rates the VDP times, not rounded ones

The wrapper reported 59.82 Hz for NTSC and a flat 50 for PAL. The VDP
times 455 x 4 master clocks a line and 263 lines (NTSC) or 313 (PAL),
and in 320 mode the slower clock and the shorter line cancel to the same
period: 59.826105 and 49.920128 Hz, the rates Beetle Saturn reports with
its own patch. The panel mode this core selects is cut to twice the
exact rate, 119.652237 Hz, and 59.82 missed it by 100 ppm - a repeated
frame every 10 seconds.

--- a/apps/ymir-libretro/src/libretro.cpp
+++ b/apps/ymir-libretro/src/libretro.cpp
@@ -1178,7 +1178,12 @@ RETRO_API void retro_get_system_av_info(struct retro_system_av_info *info) {
     info->geometry.max_height = ymir::vdp::kMaxResV;
     info->geometry.aspect_ratio = 4.0f / 3.0f;
 
-    info->timing.fps = core.is_pal ? 50.0 : 59.82;
+    // The rates the VDP times: 455 x 4 master clocks a line, 263 lines
+    // (NTSC) or 313 (PAL), over the 352-mode master clock - the 320-mode
+    // clock and line length cancel to the same period. 59.826105 and
+    // 49.920128 Hz; 59.82 missed the panel mode cut to twice the rate.
+    info->timing.fps = core.is_pal ? ymir::sys::kPALClock / (455.0 * 4 * 313)
+                                   : ymir::sys::kNTSCClock / (455.0 * 4 * 263);
     info->timing.sample_rate = 44100.0;
 }
 
